## Contract-major 3: ES256 grants and proofs

Contract-major 3 (`BoundedAuthorityProtocol.V3`,
[specification](https://hexdocs.pm/bounded_authority_protocol/bap-v3.html)) is the
`BAP3-ES256-SHA256` suite: ECDSA over P-256 with SHA-256. Grants and proofs carry `v: 3` and
`alg: "ES256"`, the holder key travels as an EC JWK, and a signature is the raw 64-byte `r || s`
form of RFC 7518 § 3.4 with `s` in the low half (`s <= n/2`). `BoundedAuthorityProtocol.V3` has
its own grant and proof producers; the trusted-issuer, expected-context, and credentials structs
are the ones the demonstration setup used.

`:crypto`, like most KMS and HSM interfaces, returns an ECDSA signature in DER and may return
either `s`. The signer converts it with `BoundedAuthorityProtocol.Es256.der_to_raw/1` and then
`BoundedAuthorityProtocol.Es256.normalize_low_s/1` before assembly. Assembly itself never
normalizes; it refuses a high-S signature.

```elixir
notebook_value = (
  alias BoundedAuthorityProtocol.Es256
  alias BoundedAuthorityProtocol.V3
  alias BoundedAuthorityProtocol.V3.EcJwk

  {es_issuer_public, es_issuer_private} = :crypto.generate_key(:ecdh, :prime256v1)
  {es_holder_public, es_holder_private} = :crypto.generate_key(:ecdh, :prime256v1)

  es256_sign = fn message, private_key ->
    der = :crypto.sign(:ecdsa, :sha256, message, [private_key, :prime256v1])
    {:ok, raw} = Es256.der_to_raw(der)
    {:ok, low_s} = Es256.normalize_low_s(raw)
    low_s
  end

  {:ok, es_holder_thumbprint} = EcJwk.public_key_thumbprint_raw(es_holder_public, %{})

  es_grant = %V3.Grant{
    key_id: "es-issuer-1",
    issuer: "https://issuer.example",
    grant_id: "grant-2026-es-001",
    audiences: ["https://service.example"],
    issued_at: 1_800_000_000,
    not_before: 1_800_000_000,
    expires_at: 1_800_003_600,
    holder_thumbprint: es_holder_thumbprint,
    operations: [
      %V3.Operation{
        name: "start_job",
        selectors: [
          {:equals, ["job", "queue"], {:string, "batch"}},
          {:lte, ["job", "gpu_hours"], {:integer, 8}}
        ]
      }
    ]
  }

  {:ok, es_grant_input} = V3.grant_signing_input(es_grant, %{})

  {:ok, es_grant_compact} =
    V3.assemble_compact(es_grant_input, es256_sign.(es_grant_input.message, es_issuer_private))

  es_arguments =
    {:object,
     [{"job", {:object, [{"queue", {:string, "batch"}}, {"gpu_hours", {:integer, 4}}]}}]}

  es_proof = %V3.Proof{
    holder_public_key: es_holder_public,
    proof_id: "proof-2026-es-001",
    method: "POST",
    target_uri: "https://service.example/jobs",
    issued_at: now,
    nonce: nil,
    invocation_id: "7d444840-9dc0-11ed-a8fc-0242ac120004",
    operation: "start_job",
    grant_compact: es_grant_compact,
    cast_arguments: es_arguments
  }

  {:ok, es_proof_input} = V3.proof_signing_input(es_proof, %{})
  es_proof_signature = es256_sign.(es_proof_input.message, es_holder_private)
  {:ok, es_proof_compact} = V3.assemble_compact(es_proof_input, es_proof_signature)

  es_trusted = %TrustedIssuer{key_id: "es-issuer-1", public_key: es_issuer_public}
  es_credentials = %Credentials{grant: es_grant_compact, proof: es_proof_compact}

  es_expected = %ExpectedRequest{
    trusted_issuer: es_trusted,
    issuer: "https://issuer.example",
    audience: "https://service.example",
    method: "POST",
    target_uri: "https://service.example/jobs",
    invocation_id: "7d444840-9dc0-11ed-a8fc-0242ac120004",
    operation: "start_job",
    cast_arguments: es_arguments,
    evaluation_time: now,
    clock_skew: 60,
    proof_max_age: 300,
    nonce: :not_required,
    bounds: %{}
  }

  {:ok, es_grant_facts} = V3.verify_grant(es_grant_compact, es_trusted, expected_grant)
  {:ok, es_envelope_facts} = V3.check_envelope(es_credentials, es_expected)

  %{
    grant: Map.take(Map.from_struct(es_grant_facts), [:version, :grant_id, :authorization]),
    envelope: Map.take(Map.from_struct(es_envelope_facts), [:operation, :authorization])
  }
)
true = notebook_value === (
  %{
    grant: %{version: 3, grant_id: "grant-2026-es-001", authorization: :not_evaluated},
    envelope: %{operation: "start_job", authorization: :not_evaluated}
  }
)
notebook_value
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
%{
  grant: %{version: 3, grant_id: "grant-2026-es-001", authorization: :not_evaluated},
  envelope: %{operation: "start_job", authorization: :not_evaluated}
}
```

## ES256 attacks fail closed

ECDSA signatures are malleable: if `(r, s)` verifies, so does `(r, n - s)`. Contract-major 3
accepts only the low-`s` member of each pair (`REQ3-SIGNING-low-s`). Below, the backend alone
accepts the high-S twin of the holder signature, and `check_envelope` refuses it. The `Es256`
helpers turn the twin's DER form back into the original low-S signature, which is what a signer
does with whatever its KMS or HSM returns.

Each contract-major parses only its own bytes (`REQ3-CORE-cross-major-reject`). Decoding takes no
key, so the cross-major attempts below use `decode_grant` and `decode_proof`: the contract-major 3
decoders refuse the grant and proof of the contract-major 1 envelope from the demonstration setup, and the
contract-major 1 and 2 decoders refuse the contract-major 3 grant and proof. The
`same_major_decodes` entries show each set of bytes decoding under its own major, so the
refusals come from the major check alone. The last attempt presents the contract-major 3 grant
with a proof signed by a key the grant does not name.

```elixir
notebook_value = (
  # The P-256 group order (contract-major 3 specification § 3.2):
  n = 0xFFFFFFFF00000000FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFBCE6FAADA7179E84F3B9CAC2FC632551

  <<es_r::256, es_s::256>> = es_proof_signature
  high_s_signature = <<es_r::256, n - es_s::256>>

  high_s_proof =
    es_proof_input.message <> "." <> Base.url_encode64(high_s_signature, padding: false)

  # The backend verifies DER, so frame the twin as a DER ECDSA-Sig-Value
  # (SEQUENCE { INTEGER r, INTEGER s }; a leading zero byte keeps an INTEGER positive):
  der_integer = fn integer ->
    bytes = :binary.encode_unsigned(integer)
    bytes = if :binary.first(bytes) >= 0x80, do: <<0>> <> bytes, else: bytes
    <<0x02, byte_size(bytes)>> <> bytes
  end

  high_s_body = der_integer.(es_r) <> der_integer.(n - es_s)
  high_s_der = <<0x30, byte_size(high_s_body)>> <> high_s_body

  backend_accepts_high_s_twin =
    :crypto.verify(:ecdsa, :sha256, es_proof_input.message, high_s_der, [
      es_holder_public,
      :prime256v1
    ])

  # A different P-256 key presents the same grant with a correctly signed proof of its own:
  {other_public, other_private} = :crypto.generate_key(:ecdh, :prime256v1)
  {:ok, other_input} = V3.proof_signing_input(%{es_proof | holder_public_key: other_public}, %{})

  {:ok, other_proof} =
    V3.assemble_compact(other_input, es256_sign.(other_input.message, other_private))

  decodes? = &match?({:ok, _decoded}, &1)

  %{
    backend_accepts_high_s_twin: backend_accepts_high_s_twin,
    helpers_recover_low_s:
      with({:ok, raw} <- Es256.der_to_raw(high_s_der), do: Es256.normalize_low_s(raw)) ==
        {:ok, es_proof_signature},
    same_major_decodes: %{
      major_one_grant: decodes?.(BoundedAuthorityProtocol.V1.decode_grant(grant_compact, %{})),
      major_one_proof: decodes?.(BoundedAuthorityProtocol.V1.decode_proof(proof_compact, %{})),
      major_three_grant: decodes?.(V3.decode_grant(es_grant_compact, %{})),
      major_three_proof: decodes?.(V3.decode_proof(es_proof_compact, %{}))
    },
    rejections: %{
      high_s:
        V3.check_envelope(%Credentials{grant: es_grant_compact, proof: high_s_proof}, es_expected),
      major_one_grant_through_major_three: V3.decode_grant(grant_compact, %{}),
      major_one_proof_through_major_three: V3.decode_proof(proof_compact, %{}),
      major_three_grant_through_major_one:
        BoundedAuthorityProtocol.V1.decode_grant(es_grant_compact, %{}),
      major_three_proof_through_major_one:
        BoundedAuthorityProtocol.V1.decode_proof(es_proof_compact, %{}),
      major_three_grant_through_major_two:
        BoundedAuthorityProtocol.V2.decode_grant(es_grant_compact, %{}),
      major_three_proof_through_major_two:
        BoundedAuthorityProtocol.V2.decode_proof(es_proof_compact, %{}),
      wrong_holder_key:
        V3.check_envelope(%Credentials{grant: es_grant_compact, proof: other_proof}, es_expected)
    }
  }
)
true = notebook_value === (
  %{
    backend_accepts_high_s_twin: true,
    helpers_recover_low_s: true,
    same_major_decodes: %{
      major_one_grant: true,
      major_one_proof: true,
      major_three_grant: true,
      major_three_proof: true
    },
    rejections: %{
      high_s: {:error, :invalid},
      major_one_grant_through_major_three: {:error, :invalid},
      major_one_proof_through_major_three: {:error, :invalid},
      major_three_grant_through_major_one: {:error, :invalid},
      major_three_proof_through_major_one: {:error, :invalid},
      major_three_grant_through_major_two: {:error, :invalid},
      major_three_proof_through_major_two: {:error, :invalid},
      wrong_holder_key: {:error, :invalid}
    }
  }
)
notebook_value
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
%{
  backend_accepts_high_s_twin: true,
  helpers_recover_low_s: true,
  same_major_decodes: %{
    major_one_grant: true,
    major_one_proof: true,
    major_three_grant: true,
    major_three_proof: true
  },
  rejections: %{
    high_s: {:error, :invalid},
    major_one_grant_through_major_three: {:error, :invalid},
    major_one_proof_through_major_three: {:error, :invalid},
    major_three_grant_through_major_one: {:error, :invalid},
    major_three_proof_through_major_one: {:error, :invalid},
    major_three_grant_through_major_two: {:error, :invalid},
    major_three_proof_through_major_two: {:error, :invalid},
    wrong_holder_key: {:error, :invalid}
  }
}
```

The high-S proof was framed by hand. A contract-major 3 verifier rejects it whatever produced
it, and a conforming signer never emits it.
